{
  "_meta": {
    "description": "Town job-board definitions + daily/weekly rotation. Authoritative source = APK il2cpp `JobData` / `JobPool` / `JobDuelBossList` (ScriptableObject, `BGS.Game.Quests`), cross-checked against prod /quests captures and UESP Blades:Jobs. Consumed by server/src/quest.rs `jobs_gen`, which loads this whole file as a raw serde_json::Value (unknown keys are ignored, so it is safe to add documentation/back-office blocks).",
    "authoritative": "jobPools[], globals (JobData scalars), perTypeDifficulty (JobData.PerTypeData.JobDifficultyDistributionWithLevel), perTypeAndSourceData (boss loot tables), jobDuelBossList, spawn-group IDs. All read directly from the compiled client.",
    "guessed": "The `jobTypes` catalog labels/objective-count hints and the level>=60 difficulty extrapolation rows are annotated `_guessed:true` where present. `dailyRotation` documents behaviour already implemented in quest.rs; the numbers there (slot counts) are authoritative from JobData, the seeding scheme is our deterministic impl choice.",
    "enums": {
      "jobType": {
        "_source": "il2cpp Job.JobType (TypeDefIndex 11096) — CORRECTED: type 2 is Fetch, NOT 'Clear'.",
        "0": "Defeat  — defeat enemies + collect reward",
        "1": "Explore — defeat the boss and find the exit",
        "2": "Fetch   — fetch objective items (rare in captures)",
        "3": "Rescue  — rescue townsfolk and defeat the boss",
        "4": "Gather  — gather items and defeat the boss",
        "5": "Duel    — win against a gladiator (duel boss)",
        "6": "COUNT (sentinel)",
        "100": "None (sentinel)"
      },
      "jobSource": {
        "_source": "il2cpp JobSource (TypeDefIndex 11901) — CORRECTED from prior draft labels.",
        "0": "None",
        "1": "Regular (the four rolling Normal-job slots)",
        "2": "Daily (one Daily job, refreshes at the daily reset)",
        "3": "Weekly (one Weekly job, refreshes Monday)"
      },
      "presentation": {
        "_source": "il2cpp Job.JobPresentation (TypeDefIndex 11097) — CORRECTED from prior draft labels.",
        "0": "Standard (the Regular/Normal rolling slots)",
        "1": "Daily (the featured Daily job)",
        "2": "Weekly (the featured Weekly boss job)",
        "3": "Special",
        "100": "None"
      },
      "recurrenceType": {
        "_source": "il2cpp Recurrence.RecurrenceType.",
        "1": "daily",
        "2": "weekly"
      },
      "jobDifficulty": {
        "_source": "il2cpp JobDifficulty enum (TypeDefIndex 11120) — the 0..4 'skull' rating the UI shows.",
        "0": "VeryEasy",
        "1": "Easy",
        "2": "Normal",
        "3": "Hard",
        "4": "VeryHard"
      },
      "dayOfWeek": "0=Sunday .. 6=Saturday (matches quest.rs weekday_sun0; il2cpp uses Recurrence.JavaDayOfWeek)"
    },
    "notes": [
      "jobPoolId values are the real APK Uids (JobPool._uid). The presentation field on each pool selects the board slot: presentation 0 = the four rolling Normal slots (maxActive 4); presentation 2 = the weekly Duel boss; presentation 1 = per-weekday featured Daily pools.",
      "endTime/nextStartTime are DERIVED at runtime from recurrence by quest.rs jobs_gen::pool_timers; this file gives only the cadence (durationSecs/resetHour/resetMinute/type/dayOfWeek).",
      "The per-instance jobSetup runtime shape (enemy spawn groups, counts, boss loot per type/source, difficulty level, gem-skip, duel boss) is GENERATED per character+day by jobs_gen::roll_job from these definitions plus the harvested constant pools baked into quest.rs (dungeon templates, enemy families, duel bosses, gather items). It is not a static table.",
      "DIFFICULTY SCALING: quest.rs jobs_gen::roll_difficulty reads perTypeDifficulty[jobType].difficultyByLevel, picks the highest row whose level <= player level, and rolls difficultyLevel = playerLevel + rand(veryEasyMin .. veryHardMax) clamped to >=1. The client then maps difficultyLevel-vs-playerLevel into the 0..4 skull rating via the veryEasyMin/easyMin/normalMin/hardMin/veryHardMin thresholds (il2cpp QuestDifficultyCalculator.GetRelativeDifficulty). So raising these offsets makes a level band harder.",
      "AUTO-EASING: UESP notes that after repeated failed jobs the game lowers difficulty. That live-adjust is character state (not in this file); a faithful server can decrement a per-character difficulty bias — see dailyRotation.autoEasing below (currently GUESSED, not yet implemented in quest.rs)."
    ]
  },
